SUMMARY:Reiss Ellis Beckles presents Blues and The Abstract Truth
DESCRIPTION:Doors 7:45 PM\, Music 8:30 PM - 2 sets of music\n \nLine-up:\nJoseph Oti - Trumpet\nReiss Ellis Beckles - Alto Saxophone\nHouston Patton - Tenor Saxophone\nPhil Knights - Baritone Saxophone\nSimon Purcell - Piano\nTom Riviere - Double Bass\nLaura Klain - Drum Kit\nAbout:\nFor one night only\, saxophonist and bandleader Reiss Ellis Beckles presents a live performance of Oliver Nelson’s iconic The Blues and the Abstract Truth. Featuring Nelson’s original arrangements\, the ensemble brings this landmark 1961 recording to life in its entirety — celebrating its powerful melodies\, sophisticated harmonies and timeless blues language. A rare opportunity to experience one of jazz’s most influential albums performed live\, as originally conceived.
URL:https://www.vortexjazz.co.uk/event/reiss-ellis-beckles-presents-blues-and-the-abstract-truth/
LOCATION:11 Gillett Square\, London\, N16 8AZ
GEO:51.5487082;-0.0764992
