SUMMARY:Miles Spilsbury
DESCRIPTION:Doors 7:45 PM\, Music 8:30 PM - 2 sets of music\n \nLine-up:\nMiles Spilsbury - Tenor saxophone\, Soprano Saxophone\, EWI\, Flute\, Electronics\, Synthesiser\, Sampling\nHarvey Grant - Synthesizer\, Keytar\, Electronics\nRosie Turton - Modular Synthesiser\nJake Long - Modified Drum Kit\, Percussion\nCam Dawson - Bass Guitar\nAbout\nMiles Spilsbury makes warm & expansive music\, inspired by great improvising ensembles and drawing from fusion & new age worlds. His collaborators include Carlos Niño\, Puma Blue\, Nate Mercereau\, Surya Botofasina & Gorse Panshawe as well as playing in The Physics House Band & Spirit Level.\n\nFollowing on from his debut album ‘Light Manoeuvres’ and recent release ‘Spirit Level’\, the multi instrumentalist & composer presents new music and improvisations with a quintet. Spilsbury holds the two sometimes contrasting approaches of pure improvisation\, and carefully constructed compositions and explores both without genre constraint.\n\nWith influences ranging from Jon Hassell\, Don Cherry\, Billy Harper\, Iasos & Art Ensemble Of Chicago\, the group will explore textural improvisation with experimental instrumentation.\n\n \n\n[embed]https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T2NUpYNI73s[/embed]
URL:https://www.vortexjazz.co.uk/event/miles-spilsbury/
LOCATION:11 Gillett Square\, London\, N16 8AZ
GEO:51.5487082;-0.0764992
