SUMMARY:Jure Pukl - ANALOG AI (Two Shows)
DESCRIPTION:Timings:\n*Please note each ticket will give you access to the time slot you book for. Please arrive for the door time.\n1st Show\nDoors 7:00 PM\, Music 7:30 PM – 1 set of music\n2nd Show\nDoors 9:30 PM\, Music 10:00 PM – 1 set of music\n\n\n\nLine-up:\nJure Pukl - Tenor saxophone & Soprano Saxophone\nJohn Escreet - Piano\nJoe Sanders - Double bass\nChristian Lillinger - Drum kit\n\n \nAbout:\nA musical imitation of analogue artificial intelligence.  Broken\, technically sophisticated rhythms\, modern lyrical bass lines\, robust saxophone sounds and unpredictable improvisation constitutes the language of this new band of old friends. Their musical expression is a response to AI\, as they insist that music is still at it's most powerful\, beautiful\, most wild\, lyrical and sensual when performed by musicians in the moment and before a live audience. After making his highly praised albums 'Broken Circles’ and ‘Melt’ (Whirlwind Recordings)\, Jure Pukl\, one of Slovenia's most acclaimed musicians and his project Analog AI are embarking on a tour to present the material from their forthcoming album.\n\n \n\n
